alerte CMD AND ENTRYPONIT


to run docker without sudo i need to add the user to the docker group with sudo usermod -aG docker $user
if i want to install and image form docker hub docker pull name of images
to see runing continers docker ps
to see all continers including stoped ones docker ps -a
if i want to run a continer i do docker run image name 
if i want to run a continer in the background docker run -d image name () and the docker return a generate continer name
if i want to set a name by my self docker run --name setname image name
if i want to stop a continer docker stop (continer name or continer id)
if i want to change the port docker run -p 8080:80
if i want to delete a continer docker rm -f (force if the continer is runing)
if i want to start an existing continer docker start (name or id of continer)
if i want a new continer docker run 
and then if i want to delete image so docker rmi name of image
so if i want to run a command inside an existing container docker exec container-name executable commnad like ls
and if i want to ineracet with a shell process so i add -it remamber exec start a process inside my container
and if i want logs of my container docker logs container-name
and if i want detailed information about the container docker inspect container-name 